---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { bookedArtistSystemConfig } from '../data/booked-artist-system';
const { supportEmail, price, guaranteeDays } = bookedArtistSystemConfig;
const supportHref = `mailto:${supportEmail}`;
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Use" description="Terms for the Tatassist website, free resources, and one-time digital product." pageType="terms">
  <Nav slot="header" />
  <section class="pt-28 sm:pt-36 pb-12 sm:pb-16 bg-brand-dark border-b border-white/5">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-brand-gold text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Clear expectations</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-cream leading-tight mb-5">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">These terms cover the Tatassist website and free resources. The product-specific terms below govern a purchase of The Booked Artist System.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-brand-text-muted mt-6">Updated September 4, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="py-14 sm:py-20 bg-brand-dark">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6"><div class="prose-tatassist max-w-none">
      <h2>The current launch purchase</h2>
      <p>The Booked Artist System is offered at a <strong>${price} one-time launch price</strong>. It is not a membership, reservation, or subscription. Stripe provides the current checkout. The amount displayed at checkout and the files listed on the sales page identify the purchase.</p>
      <p>The <a href="/booked-artist-system-terms">Booked Artist System Product Terms</a> cover delivery, the individual business license, and the <a href="/booked-artist-system-terms#refunds">{guaranteeDays}-day satisfaction guarantee</a>. Those product-specific terms control for that purchase.</p>
      <h2>Earlier purchases and other offers</h2>
      <p>An earlier reservation, membership, or other product remains subject to the terms agreed at its original checkout. The current launch does not change an existing subscription, its price, paid access, cancellation rights, or refund rights. Contact <a href={supportHref}>{supportEmail}</a> for help with an earlier transaction.</p>
      <h2>Business education, not professional advice</h2>
      <p>Tatassist provides informational business education, examples, worksheets, and adaptable templates for tattoo artists. Nothing we publish is legal, medical, tax, accounting, employment, safety, or regulatory advice. Policy tools help you make business decisions; they are not ready-to-publish legal forms or a promise of compliance.</p>
      <p>You are responsible for reviewing and adapting materials for your business, clients, software, and location, and for obtaining qualified professional advice when needed. Do not send client health records, identification, signatures, or consent records to Tatassist.</p>
      <h2>License and ownership</h2>
      <p>Unless an offer expressly says otherwise, a purchase licenses one working artist to adapt and use the included materials in that artist's own tattoo business. You may customize working copies and client-facing language. You may not resell, redistribute, sublicense, publish the files as your own product, or upload them to a shared template library. Contact support for multi-artist studio use.</p>
      <h2>No guaranteed results</h2>
      <p>Tatassist does not guarantee bookings, revenue, profit, deposits, client response, time savings, or any other business result. Results depend on your market, work, pricing, audience, implementation, and decisions. A founder's personal experience is not a promise of your result.</p>
      <h2>External services</h2>
      <p>Checkout and email services operate under their own terms and privacy practices. Tatassist does not collect or store your full payment-card number on this website. See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for information about website data and service providers.</p>
      <h2>Acceptable use and availability</h2>
      <p>Do not misuse the site, interfere with its operation, attempt unauthorized access, violate another person's rights, or use Tatassist content unlawfully. We may suspend access for material misuse, nonpayment, account sharing, resale, or other breach, while honoring applicable paid-access and refund rights.</p>
      <h2>Disclaimers and responsibility</h2>
      <p>The site and materials are provided on an as-available basis to the extent permitted by law. You are responsible for your business decisions, communications, policies, data handling, and compliance. To the extent permitted by law, Tatassist is not responsible for indirect, incidental, special, or consequential losses arising from use of the site or materials.</p>
      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>Updates are identified by the date above. These updates do not retroactively remove rights attached to an earlier purchase. Questions about terms, access, billing, or refunds can be sent to <a href={supportHref}>{supportEmail}</a>.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
